<title>PERU: Peru's net int'l reserves off to $9.087 billion.</title>
<headline>Peru's net int'l reserves off to $9.087 billion.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said Friday its net international reserves fell to $9.087 billion on February 26 from $9.118 billion the previous week.</p>
<p>Reserves ended 1996 at $8.540 billion.</p>
<p>((-- Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
